{
  "_comment": [
    "Per-skill environment policy (night M1, GUARD1; gap analysis §7.3.5, spec §5 item 6).",
    "Gating is DATA, not a new frontmatter key: G24's `surfaces:` registry is untouched.",
    "One row per directory under skills/ - the key set IS sorted(os.listdir('skills')),",
    "pinned by tests/run_env_detect_test.py, so a new skill without a row is a red.",
    "full = the skill runs as shipped. degraded = it runs with the part that needs the",
    "missing surface named and skipped. refuse = it declines in one plain sentence.",
    "merged_cloud: only the five `surfaces: cowork` skills differ; every other skill is",
    "`full` because it degrades at the access layer, not by policy.",
    "unknown (§0.34): a READER proceeds behind a banner line; a WRITER refuses. The",
    "writer set is derived, never hand-listed - a skill is a writer iff its SKILL.md",
    "carries a `## Writer Contract` section."
  ],
  "modes": [
    "legacy_cowork",
    "merged_cloud",
    "claude_code_local",
    "unknown"
  ],
  "policies": [
    "full",
    "degraded",
    "refuse"
  ],
  "default": "full",
  "writer_marker": "## Writer Contract",
